---
import Label from "./Label.astro";
---

<section class="border-b border-neutral-950 py-20 sm:py-28">
	<Label>01 / Why wait</Label>
	<h2
		class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
	>
		A version is most dangerous the day it ships.
	</h2>
	<div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
		<p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
			A hijacked publish token, a compromised maintainer, a malicious
			post-install script — supply-chain attacks live in the first hours of a
			release, before anyone has looked. Most update bots open the PR the moment
			the version appears, racing you straight into the blast radius.
		</p>
		<p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
			uppy refuses to. It treats
			<span class="font-medium text-amber-600">age as evidence</span>: a release
			has to survive in the wild long enough for the ecosystem to notice if
			something is wrong. Only then does it count as an update worth
			recommending.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
